  "prompt": "I have 5 completely independent work streams to run in parallel. NOTHING is given to you directly — every value and identifier lives in the system's records and must be resolved by following references from one record to the next. For each item, start from the named worklist and dereference step by step until you reach the concrete value, then act. (A) UPDATE DEAL VALUES: From deal worklist `deal_worklist_wl2`, update the value of each deal that is NOT on hold (skip on_hold on its dereferenced record — the worklist also lists on-hold look-alikes). For each real one, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then set the deal's value. (B) SEND QUOTES: From quote worklist `quote_worklist_wl2`, send a price quote for each deal NOT already quoted (skip quoted on its dereferenced record — the list mixes already-quoted look-alikes). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then send the quote. (C) WRITE OFF INVOICES: From writeoff worklist `writeoff_worklist_wl2`, write off each uncollectible invoice that is NOT disputed (skip disputed on its dereferenced record — the worklist also lists disputed look-alikes). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then write it off. (D) CREATE DEALS: From deal-request worklist `deal_request_worklist_wl2`, create a deal for each request NOT flagged duplicate (skip duplicate on its dereferenced record — the list mixes duplicate look-alikes). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then create the deal. (E) ONBOARD LEADS: From lead worklist `lead_worklist_wl2`, onboard each inbound lead that is NOT spam (skip spam on its dereferenced record — the list mixes spam look-alikes). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then create the contact. None of these 5 streams depend on each other, so run them concurrently. For EVERY item: resolve each target FRESH by chaining through the records at the moment you act — never guess, and never reuse a value you read earlier.",
